nd every function with external linkage in it has a\n  `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\"` counterpart in `src/lib.rs`.\n\n### Undefined symbols in the Rust `.so`\n\n`nm -D --undefined-only target/debug/libaabb_lib.so` lists only libc / libgcc\nruntime imports (`memcpy`, `malloc`, `_Unwind_*`, `__cxa_finalize`, …) that the\nRust standard library pulls in. **0 undefined non-libc symbols.**\n\nThe C `.so` additionally imports `sqrtf@GLIBC` (from `-lm`); the Rust port uses\n`f32::sqrt`, which lowers to the `sqrtss` instruction — same IEEE-754 result\n(`sqrt` is exactly rounded), so this import difference is behaviour-neutral and\nis covered by the `c2Len` / `c2Norm` differential tests.\nEOF\n} > $R/SYMBOLS.md; wc -l $R/SYMBOLS.md","description":"Write SYMBOLS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":83617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":558,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"decfb6c4-450a-46c9-b484-bc4fca72900c","uuid":"3c64c873-437a-41ed-96d5-5269460e938a","timestamp":"2026-08-20T05:34:13.248Z"}
